{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/490435-contracts-of-elements-sharks-are-not-an-element","id":490435,"title":"Contracts of Elements: Sharks are not an element","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-24T06:17:04-07:00","id":490435,"title":"Contracts of Elements: Sharks are not an element","content":"As part of a long-running semi-live-action Changeling game I run, I've had to make frequent calls on what is and isn't an element (for the purposes of Contracts of Elements). The book names some things that are traditional (like fire, water, air, wood, metal, and earth), some things that are sensible (like ice), and some that are just odd (like light and pollution). Some players have asked for increasingly ludicrous things to be elements (including pants, mayonnaise, surprise, and, most frequently, sharks) to the point where I made a flowchart to tell if something was an element or not. The rules I use boil down to: it must be a homogeneous, tangible, mass noun to qualify. If it's not tangible, it can't be conceptual (so light can be an element, but surprise can't). It can't be too broad (like matter) or too narrow (like mayonnaise). And you can pick something weird (like anti-matter or void) but it still follows the parameters set in the book, and good luck fulfilling the catch.<br /> <br /> I'm interested in other folk's calls about what is and isn't an element (again, for the purposes of the 1e contract).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T08:08:42-07:00","id":490569,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:20px\">Edited to incorporate AceOfAlmonds' advice.</span><br /> <br /> Believe it or not, Time and Space can be elements.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:24px\">For Control Time:</span><br /> <br /> 1st clause: protects against magic designed to slow you down, freeze you in time or rapidly age you.<br /> <br /> 2nd clause: whatever you attack ages and rots rapidly. You are enveloped by clouds of rust and corpse gas. The original Catch becomes null, as sources of time do not exist. Instead you may, you may allow your sense of time to be altered for the scene, reducing all dice pool for Remembering to 1/3, round up.<br /> <br /> 3rd clause: make yourself faster and others slower. You gain 2 Defense OR 2 Initiative. Exceptional Success: you guide the flow of time with such finesse that you may declare your attacks as reflexive actions, which means that each turn you may attack and do something else, EXCEPT attack again. This lasts for a number of turns equal to Wyrd/2 round up. Imagine a maniacal changeling with a Hollow full of Hedgespun automatons that resemble clockwork and were imbued with many twitching eyes and hearts that beat audibly, just so he can fulfill this Catch whenever an intruder walks in.<br /> <br /> 4th clause: becomes null. Instead of &quot;summoning&quot; Time, ask it to make Remembering rolls gain a bonus equal to your Wyrd for the scene. Cannot be used to cancel the penalty inflicted by the Catch of the second clause.<br /> <br /> 5th clause: You may become fluid by turning into an intangible mass of clockwork. The fluid form may also look like water, quicksilver or sand. Either way, most attacks go right through you. Cancelling the fluid form requires you to attack the changeling with something that opposes Time. What is the main aspect of Time in the eyes of the Wyrd? It brings change. Any object representing stability, idleness and the status quo works to cancel the changeling's fluid form.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><span style=\"font-size:24px\">For Control Space:</span></span><br /> <br /> 1st clause: protects against twisted spaces, being teleported into other locations and locked into a pocket dimension.<br /> <br /> 2nd clause: whatever you attack is warped by space like a Picasso painting or fractal art, and so are you. The original Catch becomes null, as sources of space do not exist. Instead, you may allow your sense of space to be altered for the scene, reducing all dice pool for Perception to 1/3, round up.<br /> <br /> 3rd clause: bend space around your attackers. You gain 2 Defense OR 2 Initiative. Exceptional Success: you bend space so strongly that you can attack many opponents at once during this turn. On a successful attack, multiply your total damage by your Wyrd. You then distribute the damage points among your opponents, but each opponent may only receive damage up to your base successes. Imagine a paranoid changeling with a Hollow full of maps, telescopes and binoculars just so he can fulfill this Catch.<br /> <br /> 4th clause: becomes null. Instead of &quot;summoning&quot; Space, ask it to make Perception rolls gain a bonus equal to your Wyrd for the scene. Cannot be used to cancel the penalty inflicted by the Catch of the second clause.<br /> <br /> 5th: you may assume a fluid form of bars made of an intangible material that are connected through non-euclidean angles. The fluid form may also look like a three dimensional, humanoid wormhole. Either way, most attacks go right through you. Cancelling this fluid form requires you to attack the changeling with something that opposes Space. What is the main aspect of Space, both in the eyes of science and the Wyrd? Space requires at last two subjects to have meaning. Any object that represents unity/oneness works to cancel the fluid form of the changeling.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:24px\">For Communion With Both:</span><br /> <br /> Since Space and Time are intrinsic parts of the universe, you may Commune with either under any circumstance. However, each clause costs 1 extra glamour to activate.<br /> <br /> 1st clause: Space and Time count as intangible elements.<br /> <br /> 2nd clause: The Catch might include fixing a clock for Time, or taking the measurements of a relatively small structure.<br /> <br /> 3rd: Space and Time are ubiquitous, so the range is Wyrd x 30 yards. You may bend Time and Space in minor ways, such as making bullets miss a target, make a thrown object land in the right/wrong place and give penalties/bonuses to Physical rolls. The Catch might include building a clock or measuring a larger structure.<br /> <br /> 4th: you summon a servant that is much like the forms described in the fifth clauses of Control The Elements, but it is tangible. The Catch might include building a complex clock or measuring even larger structures.<br /> <br /> 5th: the servant has the same looks as those of the 4th clause, but may be shaped into whatever the changeling pleases. The Catch might include building a massive AND complex clock or measuring a structure inside the Hedge. Due to the Hedge's psycho-reactive nature, any structure you try to measure in order to fulfill this catch will frequently reshape itself unless somehow forced into a stable shape.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 04-24-2015, 07:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T14:32:54-07:00","id":490924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/490435-contracts-of-elements-sharks-are-not-an-element?p=490569#post490569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Believe it or not, Time and Space can be elements.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I fundamentally disagree on time and space being elements, mostly from a balance standpoint. As-written (EDIT: previous proposal), your Elemental contract suggestions are much, much more powerful than, say, Elements (Fire) or Elements (Metal). The first dot alone protects the user from all attacks, as opposed to protection from a single element (and specifically NOT from attacks). Your third-dot suggestion for time is vastly more powerful than any dots in Contracts of Hours (it's similar to the fourth dot, changing how time passes for you, but Hours 4 only works in the Hedge). The space version is also exceedingly powerful (short-range teleporting?! The closest that exists now is Dreams 5, and that requires people sleeping at the destination side and isn't instantaneous, while yours is). Both the three-dots are more powerful that similar powers at the four- or five-dot level. As for the fourth dot, with Time, getting extra scenes? That's <i>massive.</i> I wouldn't give that to an <i>Actor</i>, much less as a four-dot contract. Four-dot space has similar imbalance as the three-dot version. The fifth dot isn't as bad (although getting to choose between a solid or fluid form is more flexible than any other element), but it runs into the problem of you turning into something that represents the element, rather than the element itself.<br /> <br /> For the Communion suggestions, I'm unclear why space and time would count as air for communion; space and time are literally everywhere. Why treat them as air alone? The third dot has the same problem as the third dot in Elements; the fourth and fifth dots in Communion suffer from the same issue as Elements 5.<br /> <br /> Further, even ignoring the balance issues, time and space aren't like any of the sample elements from the book. While they do make up the universe, they're as intrinsic a part of it as gravity or matter. You can't remove them, they don't exist in discrete units. I can remove all the earth from an area, or all the air, or all the light. I can't remove time, or space.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","user":"AceOfAlmonds","date":".  post I was critiquing changed 04-25-2015, 01:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T14:51:20-07:00","id":490959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/490435-contracts-of-elements-sharks-are-not-an-element?p=490924#post490924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think I fundamentally disagree on time and space being elements, mostly from a balance standpoint. As-written, your Elemental contract suggestions are much, much more powerful than, say, Elements (Fire) or Elements (Metal). The first dot alone protects the user from all attacks, as opposed to protection from a single element (and specifically NOT from attacks). Your third-dot suggestion for time is vastly more powerful than any dots in Contracts of Hours (it's similar to the fourth dot, changing how time passes for you, but Hours 4 only works in the Hedge). The space version is also exceedingly powerful (short-range teleporting?! The closest that exists now is Dreams 5, and that requires people sleeping at the destination side and isn't instantaneous, while yours is). Both the three-dots are more powerful that similar powers at the four- or five-dot level. As for the fourth dot, with Time, getting extra scenes? That's <i>massive.</i> I wouldn't give that to an <i>Actor</i>, much less as a four-dot contract. Four-dot space has similar imbalance as the three-dot version. The fifth dot isn't as bad (although getting to choose between a solid or fluid form is more flexible than any other element), but it runs into the problem of you turning into something that represents the element, rather than the element itself.<br /> <br /> For the Communion suggestions, I'm unclear why space and time would count as air for communion; space and time are literally everywhere. Why treat them as air alone? The third dot has the same problem as the third dot in Elements; the fourth and fifth dots in Communion suffer from the same issue as Elements 5.<br /> <br /> Further, even ignoring the balance issues, time and space aren't like any of the sample elements from the book. While they do make up the universe, they're as intrinsic a part of it as gravity or matter. You can't remove them, they don't exist in discrete units. I can remove all the earth from an area, or all the air, or all the light. I can't remove time, or space.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm. You are very right. I'll see what I can do to fix the imbalance.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T15:07:36-07:00","id":490986,"title":"","content":"I think your players are messing with you for fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T10:06:51-07:00","id":491720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/490435-contracts-of-elements-sharks-are-not-an-element?p=490986#post490986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think your players are messing with you for fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I know they are. It's a combination berserk button and running gag at this stage. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> But it still got me thinking of what an element actually is (and why I would say sure, you can be a meat elemental, but once you say shark, it's a no).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","user":"AceOfAlmonds","date":".  typo'd actually 04-25-2015, 01:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T20:23:58-07:00","id":499708,"title":"","content":"... But what about laser sharks?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5875-amazonianbard","name":"AmazonianBard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5875_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T23:06:46-07:00","id":499879,"title":"","content":"Use the Contract of Elements for light and then use that for lasers on the sharks... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T12:02:54-08:00","id":792286,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure sharks fall under Fang and Talon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T12:28:27-08:00","id":792301,"title":"","content":"Depends: if the oceans in Arcadia are literally nothing but a massive collection of sharks rather than drops of water, Shark becomes an Element for that purpose.<br /> <br /> It would have to be very peculiar circumstances where I would allow that at my table, though.<br /> <br /> ...damnit, contributing to thread necromancy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T19:00:08-08:00","id":792480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/490435-contracts-of-elements-sharks-are-not-an-element?p=792301#post792301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depends: if the oceans in Arcadia are literally nothing but a massive collection of sharks rather than drops of water, Shark becomes an Element for that purpose.<br /> <br /> It would have to be very peculiar circumstances where I would allow that at my table, though.<br /> <br /> ...damnit, contributing to thread necromancy.</div> </div> </div> </div>i'm still with an picture of an ocean litteraly made of sharks in my head,what do the sharks <i>eat? </i>each other?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T19:35:03-08:00","id":792494,"title":"","content":"They eat the gumdrop buttons that rain from the sky, because Arcadia be tripping acid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T20:53:45-08:00","id":792525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/490435-contracts-of-elements-sharks-are-not-an-element?p=792494#post792494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They eat the gumdrop buttons that rain from the sky, because Arcadia be tripping acid.</div> </div> </div> </div>heh,that's why people keep coming back to arcadia in one way or another","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}